  title: [Chobani Just Brought Back This Fan-Favorite Seasonal Flavor Earlier Than Ever],
  author: [Hayley Schueneman],
  source-name: [Taste of Home],
  images: (),
  paragraphs: (
  [There’s no question that Chobani is absolutely crushing it with its coffee creamers. Every new flavor feels better than the last, and the product’s velvety texture makes for the most decadent cups of coffee. The only downside is that many of the brand’s flavors are limited-edition or seasonal, so fans wait all year for their favorites to return. (We even made a copycat cookie butter creamer to hold us over until it comes back.)],
  [Luckily, one of Chobani’s best summertime flavors is back, and it’s back two whole months early. I guess they decided that this flavor is just too delicious to keep in the vault until June!],
  [Which Chobani creamer flavor is back on shelves?],
  [The beloved Chobani S’mores Creamer is back, baby! As a certified s’mores lover, I cannot emphasize enough how delicious this is. The combo of chocolate, graham cracker and marshmallow immediately evokes summer nights spent around the campfire.],
  [Aside from the Confetti Birthday Cake flavor, this is probably the most popular of Chobani’s seasonal offerings. Except earlier this year, the brand announced that the Confetti Birthday Cake Creamer will now be a permanent addition to the lineup. Chobani … does this mean the S’mores flavor could also become permanent? I think you should consider it!],
  [How long will the creamer be available?],
  [Typically, the S’mores flavor is released in early June to usher in the start of summer. So the fact that it’s hitting shelves in April is really exciting. “Early April” is all Chobani has shared, so it should appear on retail shelves in the next few weeks.],
  [I have a theory about why Chobani bumped up the return of its S’mores flavor. Earlier this year, the brand announced a new “Flavor Drop” lineup with its most exclusive items yet. The first one was Raspberry Rose in February, and Chobani indicated that the next Flavor Drop would be in June. I’m assuming that the company didn’t want us to run out of room in our refrigerators by releasing S’mores and the new Flavor Drop at the same time.],
  [Related:],
  [I’ve Tried Countless Nondairy Creamers, and These Are the Best],
  [Panera Just Dropped 4 New Drinks, Including the Best Drink I’ve Ever Tasted],
  [Meghann Fahy Shares Her Go-To Coffee Order and Morning Routine],
  [The post Chobani Just Brought Back This Fan-Favorite Seasonal Flavor Earlier Than Ever appeared first on Taste of Home .],
),
